      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Want the rule of thumb behind that catch-up time? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:10xayk'
    '|a||A rule of thumb: the years to catch up are roughly the static loss divided by the extra growth.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Two percent over half a point a year: four years. Halve the extra growth and it takes twice as long.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:rk9p22'
    '|a||So a market can lose on today''s scorecard and still win over a lifetime, but only if its profits really buy faster progress.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ja9619'
    '|b||That ''only if'' is where I push back. Why would a safe monopoly hurry at all?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||The economist Kenneth Arrow asked just that in 1962. A monopolist with a better product mostly replaces its own profit.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:14f36ww'
    '|b||Like Kodak. Its engineer Steve Sasson built a digital camera in 1975.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1woewi'
    '|b||Kodak, living off film, was slow to sell it,':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:zh49fh'
    '|b||and went bankrupt in 2012.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2200
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1n6c5ds'
    '|a||While a newcomer, with no profit to lose, gains the whole prize. That''s Arrow''s replacement effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:4rkni4'
    '|b||So who''s right, Schumpeter or Arrow?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1y5kc4k'
    '|a||Maybe both. In British industry data, Philippe Aghion and coauthors found innovation peaks at middling competition.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:w3vdw7'
    '|a||With too little competition, the safe monopolist dozes, as Arrow said.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:m6r9e2'
    '|b||With too much, nobody keeps enough of the reward, as Schumpeter said.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ka6ouu'
    '|b||But with American data, Aamir Hashmi found no hump, just a mild slope down. So how sure are we? Contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1rpz8hw'
    '|a||Schumpeter''s case is strong where monopolies are temporary prizes, as with patents and big labs. It breaks down where a monopoly is safe from any rival.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:eh3mo9'
    '|a||So do monopolies drive innovation? A prize for inventors helps; a monopoly with nothing to fear mostly drives itself.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:wcbl24'
    '|a||Three new cases. First: a monopoly no rival can ever enter. A postal service protected by law from every rival: which side of the hump is it on? Tap it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1voojdn'
    '|a||Three new cases. First: a monopoly no rival can ever enter. A postal service protected by law from every rival: which side of the hump is it on?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Arrow''s side: with no rival to fear, standing still costs it nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5200
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Second, patents. A patent lets an inventor charge far above cost for twenty years. What is the law trading?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Lower prices today for faster innovation later: a little static efficiency is given up to buy dynamic efficiency.':
